<title>GERMANY: Four in 10 German firms see EMU delay - poll.</title>
<headline>Four in 10 German firms see EMU delay - poll.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 42 percent of German companies expect European economic and monetary union (EMU) to be delayed, according to a poll published on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The survey, published by the business magazine &quot;Impulse&quot; on its on-line service, also showed that two percent of German firms expect that monetary union, which is scheduled to start in January 1999, will never come into being.</p>
<p>The poll surveyed 400 businesses.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
